        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "GPIO_IN.cpp",
        "documentation": "Reads a GPIO input line of the Linux device. PIN is the kernel's line name (such as 'GPIO17') or '<chip>:<offset>' (such as 'gpiochip0:17'). BIAS is LIO_BIAS_NONE, LIO_BIAS_PULL_UP or LIO_BIAS_PULL_DOWN; ACTIVE_LOW inverts the level; DEBOUNCE filters bounces shorter than its time (T#0s: off). Q is the level on every call while ENABLE is TRUE and VALID is TRUE. A pin that is missing or in use gives ERROR and ERRORTEXT, and the block tries again every 0.5 s.\nExample: button(ENABLE := TRUE, PIN := 'GPIO17', BIAS := LIO_BIAS_PULL_UP, ACTIVE_LOW := TRUE, DEBOUNCE := T#10ms); pressed := button.Q;"
      },
      {
        "name": "GPIO_OUT",
        "inputs": [
