        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "GPIO_OUT.cpp",
        "documentation": "Drives a GPIO output line of the Linux device to VALUE. PIN as for GPIO_IN. DRIVE is LIO_DRIVE_PUSH_PULL, LIO_DRIVE_OPEN_DRAIN or LIO_DRIVE_OPEN_SOURCE; ACTIVE_LOW inverts the level. When the block is no longer called (PLC stop, PLC error, new upload) the line goes to ON_STOP within 100 ms or five call intervals: LIO_STOP_OFF (default), LIO_STOP_ON or LIO_STOP_HOLD. ENABLE FALSE puts it in that state too and frees the line.\nExample: lamp(ENABLE := TRUE, PIN := 'GPIO27', VALUE := alarm, ON_STOP := LIO_STOP_OFF);"
      },
      {
        "name": "PWM_OUT",
        "inputs": [
          {
            "name": "ENABLE",
            "type": "BOOL"
          },
          {
            "name": "CHIP",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
