          },
          {
            "name": "ERROR",
            "type": "USINT"
          },
          {
            "name": "ERRORTEXT",
            "type": "STRING"
          },
          {
            "name": "VALUE",
            "type": "REAL"
          },
          {
            "name": "RAW",
            "type": "LINT"
          }
        ],
        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "READ_VALUE.cpp",
        "documentation": "Reads the first number in a file under /sys/ of the Linux device every PERIOD, outside the PLC scan: a temperature from a thermal zone or hwmon, a 1-wire sensor's temperature file, any value a kernel driver shows as a file. RAW is the number, VALUE is RAW x SCALE + OFFSET. VALID is FALSE until the first reading after a start, and on an error, when VALUE and RAW keep the last good reading.\nExample: cpu(ENABLE := TRUE, PATH := '/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp', SCALE := 0.001); temperature := cpu.VALUE;"
      },
