        "inouts": [],
        "implementation": "cpp",
        "sourceFile": "IIO_READ.cpp",
        "documentation": "Reads a channel of a Linux IIO device (ADCs and other sensors with a kernel driver) every PERIOD, outside the PLC scan. DEVICE is the device's name as the driver gives it, CHANNEL the channel's file prefix (such as 'in_voltage0'). RAW is the channel's raw value and VALUE = (RAW + offset) x scale with the driver's offset and scale, in the driver's unit (such as mV). VALID is FALSE until the first reading after a start, and on an error, when VALUE and RAW keep the last good reading.\nExample: adc(ENABLE := TRUE, DEVICE := 'adc_name', CHANNEL := 'in_voltage0'); millivolts := adc.VALUE;"
      }
    ],
    "types": [
